research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-product-of-one-minus-one-over-k-is-zero.prompt.md-1837-kind: theorem
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-product-of-one-minus-one-over-k-is-zero.prompt.md-1838-title: "For $p_k \\ge 0$ the product $\\prod (1 + p_k)$ converges iff $\\sum p_k$ converges, with $1 + \\sum_{k<n} p_k \\le \\prod_{k<n}(1+p_k) \\le 1/\\bigl(1 - \\sum_{k<n} p_k\\bigr)$ when $\\sum_{k<n} p_k < 1$; for $0 \\le p_k < 1$ the product $\\prod (1 - p_k)$ converges iff $\\sum p_k$ converges and its partial products tend to $0$ otherwise; and $\\sum |p_k|$ convergent implies $\\prod (1+p_k)$ convergent"
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-product-of-one-minus-one-over-k-is-zero.prompt.md-1839-status: published
--
