research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-3740-- **Two conventions are doing work.** $A_n$ sums the $n$ terms $a_0, \dots, a_{n-1}$, so $A_0 = 0$ and $a_k = A_{k+1} - A_k$ with no shift ([[def-series]]); and the empty sum is $0$ ([[def-finite-sum]]), which is what makes $n = 1$ a genuine instance of the identity rather than a case to be excluded.
