research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-4130-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-4131-[L2] $\sum_{k\ge1}1/k^{p}$ converges if and only if $p > 1$, with $\iota(k)^{1} = \iota(k)$; and $\sum_{k \ge 1} x_k$ is the series of $j \mapsto x_{j+1}$ ([[thm-p-series-rational]], [[def-rational-power]], [[thm-nth-roots-exist]], [[def-integer-power]], [[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-4132-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log:4133:[L3] For nonnegative $p_k$: $\prod(1+p_k)$ converges if and only if $\sum p_k$ converges, and $1 + S_n \le \Pi_n$ for every $n$ ([[thm-infinite-product-criterion]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-4134-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/certifier-page-absolute-convergence-and-rearrangement.log-4135-[L4] Convergence of an infinite product, and divergence when no tail has partial products with a nonzero limit ([[def-infinite-product]]).
